        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "policy_prompt_for_action": [
    {
      "modify_from": "If above the button at approach height with open fingers, close at the same nominal approach waypoint. If above it with closed fingers and no observed contact yet, descend to its center at z=0.0075 with fingers closed.",
      "modify_to": "At approximate button hover, allow normal approach error of roughly 1–1.5 cm to proceed to the next operation, but do not treat the achieved TCP x,y as the button center. Before closing and again before pressing, estimate the button center from the current calibrated views, refining it with the wrist image. With open fingers at approximate hover, command that button-centered x,y at z=0.15 and close on arrival. With closed fingers at approximate hover and no observed contact yet, descend directly to the newly estimated button-centered x,y at z=0.0075 with fingers closed."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "Order highlighted targets red, green, blue, with same-color ties by increasing world x then y. Select the first target not already represented by lifted_count.",
      "modify_to": "Establish the fixed target order from highlight_frame: red, green, blue, then increasing world y within each color, with increasing world x for ties. Robot-right is negative y and appears on the left of the front image. Match individual identities by position as well as color; do not reorder using positions changed by handling. Interpret lifted_count as excluding the completed prefix, including any newly completed lift observed this cycle. Select the next uncounted identity before testing whether the hand is aligned for descent."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "Once above that target, descend to its center at z=0.02 and close. Allow normal approach error of roughly 1–1.5 cm rather than repeatedly commanding the hover.",
      "modify_to": "Only when the open hand is approximately aligned above the selected uncounted target, descend to its center at z=0.02 and close. Allow normal approach error of roughly 1–1.5 cm; if already aligned, descend rather than commanding another hover. An open hand at hover above a returned, counted cube must instead approach the next uncounted target at z=0.15 with fingers open."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "Every gripper-only change must include at least 2 mm of translation if its nominal waypoint would otherwise equal the reported TCP pose; use a small upward adjustment, within 5 mm.",
      "modify_to": "For every gripper-only change, first construct the nominal object-centered waypoint rather than copying the achieved TCP pose. If that waypoint already provides at least 2 mm of translation from the reported TCP pose, do not add a nudge. Otherwise add a small upward adjustment within 5 mm so that the translation is at least 2 mm."
    }
  ],
  "refused": ""
